SHOPSONE — EDITORIAL CHAMELEON (REVISION 3: PRODUCTION-READY ARCHITECTURE SPECIFICATION)
Executive Summary
The Editorial Chameleon (Revision 3) specification remediation elevates the ShopsOne universal e-commerce architecture from a conceptual design to a production-ready, highly secure, server-authoritative enterprise specification.
Building upon the robust foundation of Revision 2—which established the Universal Does Not Mean Uniform principle, industry-specific presentation profiles, a three-tier design token hierarchy, and a strict Myanmar typography validation matrix—Revision 3 rigorously hardens all system boundaries. It addresses critical distributed systems challenges, including server-authoritative inventory locks, atomic transaction boundaries, idempotent order creation, tamper-proof server-side pricing, stable cursor-based pagination, secure remote image sanitization, and strict schema-driven configuration safety.
This is a comprehensive architectural specification and remediation document. In strict compliance with execution restrictions, no source code has been modified, no repository files have been altered, no dependencies have been installed, and no production operations have been executed. All repository-dependent contracts that lack explicit local confirmation are formally classified as NOT VERIFIED.
Architectural Principles
 * Client is Untrusted; Server is Authoritative: The browser client and frontend application layer are strictly treated as untrusted rendering and interaction surfaces. No prices, discounts, delivery fees, taxes, stock levels, or final order totals calculated on the client are accepted by backend systems without strict server-side revalidation.
 * Universal Does Not Mean Uniform: A single, unified component library renders distinct, context-aware industry presentations driven entirely by structured configuration profiles (Fashion, Electronics, Cosmetics, Grocery, Home & Living, General Retail).
 * Immutability of Primitives & Tiered Separation: Design tokens, security configurations, and layout schemas follow strict cascading boundaries where lower layers (Tier 1 primitives, Zod security schemas) cannot be overridden by merchant customizations.
 * Resilience by Design: All edge cases (empty states, loading skeletons, slow networks, offline recovery, malformed payloads, and third-party image failures) are explicitly architected to prevent white-screen crashes and layout shifts.
 * Myanmar-First Bilingual Ergonomics: Typography, form controls, line heights, and touch targets are optimized natively for complex script rendering without compromising English UI elements.
