Server-Authoritative Cart & Inventory Architecture (AR-01)
 * Inventory Authority: The client frontend never decides item availability. Stock validation executes strictly within backend transaction boundaries.
 * Atomic Reservation: When initiating checkout, an atomic database transaction locks product and variant rows (SELECT ... FOR UPDATE), verifies available quantity against cart request quantity, and writes an ephemeral reservation holding stock for 15 minutes.
 * Concurrent Purchase Protection: Database row-level locks prevent race conditions when two users attempt to purchase the final unit simultaneously. The second transaction fails gracefully with a stock deficit error, prompting cart quantity re-sync.
Idempotent Order Creation (AR-02)
 * Idempotency Key Lifecycle: The client generates a cryptographically secure UUID (Idempotency-Key header) upon checkout submission.
 * Server-Side Validation: The backend checks an idempotency_keys table for existing keys. If a key exists within a 24-hour retention window, the original order response is returned immediately without re-processing payment or deducting stock.
 * Payload Consistency: Request body cryptographic hashes (SHA-256) are validated against the stored key fingerprint to reject mismatched payload retries under the same key.
Pricing & Delivery Integrity (AR-03)
 * Server-Side Calculation: The backend recalculates item unit prices, variant adjustments, active volume discounts, compare-at thresholds, subtotal, delivery fees, and final payable totals at the moment of order placement.
 * Currency Handling: All monetary calculations in MMK use integer representations (paise/cents equivalent avoided in favor of raw integer kyat amounts with safe arithmetic validation) to prevent floating-point rounding errors.
 * Price Drift Handling: If prices change between cart addition and checkout, the checkout transaction halts, returning a price-drift payload notifying the user of updated pricing before allowing re-submission.
Product Pagination & Stable Sorting (AR-04)
 * Cursor-Based Pagination: Replaces offset pagination with cursor-based pagination (cursor = base64(sort_value + id)) to prevent duplicate items or skipped records during concurrent catalog insertions and deletions.
 * Deterministic Tie-Breaker: Every sort query includes a secondary tie-breaker (ORDER BY created_at DESC, id DESC) ensuring strict stability.
 * Filter & Sort Invalidation: Changing filters or sort orders automatically invalidates existing cursors, resetting pagination to page one.
Image Security Architecture (AR-05)
 * Trusted Host Allowlist: All product and banner image URLs must resolve against a strict allowlist of approved storage domains (e.g., Supabase storage buckets, Firebase Storage, and approved merchant CDN domains). Arbitrary external domains trigger fallback rendering.
 * SSRF Prevention: Server-side image processing pipelines (if any) are restricted from fetching arbitrary remote URLs, preventing Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF).
 * Timeout & Retry Policy: Image fetch requests enforce a 5-second timeout with a maximum of 1 bounded retry before rendering the graceful monogram error fallback.
Configuration Security Architecture (AR-06)
 * Zod Schema Validation: All merchant storefront layout configurations are parsed through strict Zod schemas enforcing maximum section counts, unique section IDs, payload size limits, and allowed property types.
 * Execution Safety: Dynamic script execution, arbitrary JSX, eval functions, and unsafe HTML tags (dangerouslySetInnerHTML with un-sanitized input) are strictly barred. Unknown section types are pruned automatically.
Security Threat & Abuse Matrix
| Threat | Impact | Prevention Mechanism | Verification Evidence |
|---|---|---|---|
| Client-Side Price Tampering | Users checking out with manipulated zero prices | Server-side recalculation of all item and cart totals from authoritative database records. | Integration test verifying forged client totals are ignored by checkout API. |
| Overselling / Race Conditions | Purchasing more stock than physically available | Database row-level locking (FOR UPDATE) and atomic inventory decrement during checkout. | Concurrent multi-client load test targeting final inventory unit. |
| Duplicate Order Submission | Double charging and accidental inventory double-deduction | Cryptographic idempotency keys with 24-hour server-side uniqueness enforcement. | Repeated rapid-fire submission test with identical idempotency headers. |
| Malicious Store Config Injection | XSS or Remote Code Execution via merchant layout payload | Strict Zod schema validation stripping unknown properties and executable scripts. | Automated fuzz testing with malicious JSON configuration payloads. |
| SSRF via Remote Images | Internal network scanning through image upload/fetch endpoints | Domain allowlist validation blocking private IP ranges and unapproved hosts. | URI validation test suite against internal and malformed endpoints. |
