Regression Protection
 * API Contract Integrity: Existing API endpoints must maintain backward compatibility. Unverified contracts must undergo explicit inspection before integration.
 * State Preservation: Client-side cart state and authentication session tokens must persist across navigation and profile shifts.
 * Checkout Continuity: Existing customer checkout submission flows remain structurally undisturbed during UI layer refactoring.
Rollback & Recovery Plan
 * Change Isolation: Frontend UI presentations (Editorial Chameleon components) and backend architectural invariants are decoupled, allowing UI rollbacks without data corruption.
 * Data Integrity Checks: Database transaction logs and inventory audit trails maintain immutability. In the event of transaction failures, automatic rollbacks restore inventory counters.
 * Financial Mutations Note: Frontend deployments cannot reverse completed financial or inventory database mutations; rollbacks apply strictly to presentation layer and API routing configurations.
